 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Not weird all. Lots of people find them fascinating. Do you listen to ones about real cases, or fictional ones that feel like news stories? No problem. Do you listen to ones about real cases, or fictional ones that feel like news stories? Then you' in the majority. Many people like being dropped into a story and having to figure out whodunit. For true crime shows, no. Most victims' voices are silenced anyway, because the only record is police report. There' a lighthearted true crime genre, where the hosts poke fun at the absurdities of the situation. That's smart. Watch few episodes first so you know the style, and you can spot the serious ones from the goofy ones in seconds.",
